   "spoken": "Who owns Atari now?"
  },
  {
   "kind": "cart",
   "text": "A French company in Paris. The name has been sold five times: Warner in 1976, Jack Tramiel in 1984, Hasbro for $5 million in 1998."
  },
  {
   "kind": "props",
   "text": "Wade Rosen runs it today. Revenue reached about $65 million last year, its best in over a decade."
  },
  {
   "kind": "gallery",
   "text": "The 2600. The 7800. The Jaguar. Every one of them came from a company that kept changing hands."
  },
  {
   "kind": "crt2",
   "text": "And it still ships cartridges. The 7800 Plus arrived in 2024 at $129.99."
  },
